WEBVTT

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:30.349
after two or three hours,
you just start to hit that mark

00:02:30.373 --> 00:02:32.937
where you wish you could
kind of teleport home.

00:02:32.961 --> 00:02:35.001
You probably know
this feeling well, right?

00:02:35.025 --> 00:02:36.392
Like, there you are --

00:02:36.416 --> 00:02:37.574
CA: Oh, I do.

00:02:37.598 --> 00:02:41.397
SC:... at the wonderful TED dinner, and
then suddenly, "Oh, I wish I could go."

00:02:41.421 --> 00:02:43.874
CA: Yeah, and people assume
that because I host TED,

00:02:43.898 --> 00:02:45.121
I must be an extrovert.

00:02:45.145 --> 00:02:47.874
You know, here's this conference
with 1,500 people there,

00:02:47.898 --> 00:02:49.401
and you have these big events,

00:02:49.425 --> 00:02:52.793
and you have to go around
and glad-hand people and so forth.

00:02:52.817 --> 00:02:56.285
And people assume I must be
an extrovert, and I'm not.

00:02:56.309 --> 00:02:58.263
And that is exactly what happens to me.

00:02:58.287 --> 00:03:01.791
Actually, it's not even two hours.
It's about 74 minutes.